orrect:** by induction on `i`: `i >> 1 < i` for `i >= 1`, so the referenced entry is already correct, and appending the bit `i & 1` adds exactly that many set bits.\n\n**Common mistakes:** calling popcount per element (`O(n log n)`, acceptable but not the point); using `i / 2` with float division in Python; off-by-one on the array length (`n + 1` entries).\n\n**Interview follow-ups:** (1) Number of 1 Bits for a single value (Kernighan's trick). (2) Total number of set bits in `0..n` without the array (count contribution per bit position in `O(log n)`). (3) Same idea for counting trailing zeros or parity of each number.","complexity":{"time":"O(n)","space":"O(n) for the output"},"similar":["number-of-1-bits","single-number","power-of-two"],"number":160,"starter":"class Solution:\n    def countBits(self, n: int) -> List[int]:\n        pass\n"}